id: pm-jira-qmt4
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.7.27
description: "Raises the pm-cli peerDependency to >=2026.7.27 and the devDependency to ^2026.7.27, refreshes the lockfile, and adds a real activation proof. The three extension version sites (package.json, manifest.json and the module's own self-reported version constant) were ALREADY at 2026.7.27 on entry and are unchanged by this PR; an earlier revision of this description wrongly claimed to bump them, copied from the sibling pm-starter chore where the bump was genuinely part of the change. An activation proof is mandatory rather than optional for this bump because 2026.7.27 hardened host-owned global flags: a collision aborts command registration AT the offending command, dropping it and every later sibling, while --help still exits 0 with a misleading Commander arity error (upstream pm-cli#772). Verified on the real CLI in a throwaway workspace: install ok with no warnings, pm jira --help exits 0, host commands stay intact (pm list --json still valid), and the flag-collision audit finds no host-owned global declared."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T16:33:51.840Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T21:36:57.486Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T16:33:53.497Z"
author: claude-code
acceptance_criteria: "peerDependencies >=2026.7.27 and devDependencies ^2026.7.27 with a refreshed lockfile; package.json, manifest.json and the module version constant all read 2026.7.27; node_modules resolves 2026.7.27; pm jira --help exits 0 on the real CLI with the built extension installed; flag-collision audit clean; host pm list --json still valid; 78 tests pass."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T16:33:52.564Z",claude-code,"Gates: build, typecheck, check, 78 tests passing, changelog:full and changelog:check after git fetch --tags --force."
  "2026-07-27T16:46:27.643Z",claude-code,"CORRECTION from Greptile review: this item's description claimed the change bumps all THREE version sites, but that is inaccurate for this package. manifest.json and the module's self-reported version constant were ALREADY 2026.7.27 on main, bumped by the daily release, so this PR changes only package.json (the pm-cli dependency ranges plus the package version) and the lockfile. The three-site rule itself still holds and is why the bump script rewrites all three when they differ; it simply had nothing to do here. The claim was carried over verbatim from the pm-starter change, where manifest.json and the module constant genuinely WERE stale and a reviewer caught the drift. Verified: git diff against origin/main touches neither manifest.json nor index.ts in this package."
  "2026-07-27T21:25:59.878Z",claude-code,"CORRECTION to this item's own description, raised by Greptile on PR #42 and verified: this change did NOT bump the three version sites. git show origin/main:package.json already read 2026.7.27 before the branch, and manifest.json and the module version constant were likewise already aligned; nothing in the diff touches them. That claim was copied from the sibling pm-starter chore, where the bump was real, and it wrongly attributes an earlier release's change to this PR. What this PR actually does: raises the pm-cli peerDependency to >=2026.7.27 and the devDependency to ^2026.7.27, refreshes the lockfile, and adds the activation proof. The acceptance criterion reading 'package.json, manifest.json and the module version constant all read 2026.7.27' is still SATISFIED - it was simply already true on entry rather than achieved here. Recorded as an appended note rather than a description rewrite so both the original claim and the correction stay in the append-only history, which is the honest record for later release archaeology."
close_reason: Shipped with the activation proof the hardened 2026.7.27 host requires.
body: ""
